cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these files, please cite them as below, and cite
  Beck et al. (2023), the map they are generalised from.
type: dataset
title: "Ilhoh: generalised Köppen-Geiger climate polygons, 1991–2020"
authors:
  - given-names: Diogo
    family-names: Marques Macedo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-6977-7180"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jirodimm/Ilhoh"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Köppen-Geiger climate classes as polygons, one multipolygon per class,
  in GeoJSON and TopoJSON, generalised from the 1 km map for 1991–2020
  of Beck et al. (2023) for use in web maps.
keywords:
  - Köppen-Geiger
  - climate classification
  - GeoJSON
  - TopoJSON
references:
  - type: article
    title: "High-resolution (1 km) Köppen-Geiger maps for 1901–2099 based on constrained CMIP6 projections"
    authors:
      - given-names: Hylke E.
        family-names: Beck
      - given-names: Tim R.
        family-names: McVicar
      - given-names: Noemi
        family-names: Vergopolan
      - given-names: Alexis
        family-names: Berg
      - given-names: Nicholas J.
        family-names: Lutsko
      - given-names: Ambroise
        family-names: Dufour
      - given-names: Zhenzhong
        family-names: Zeng
      - given-names: Xin
        family-names: Jiang
      - given-names: Albert I. J. M.
        family-names: van Dijk
      - given-names: Diego G.
        family-names: Miralles
    journal: Scientific Data
    volume: 10
    start: 724
    year: 2023
    doi: 10.1038/s41597-023-02549-6
